{"id": "EUVD-2026-106901", "enisaUuid": "2cda7d24-7d4c-3bdb-a9c7-f725e41bc9bd", "description": "Dulwich from 0.22.5 before 1.2.8 contains a path traversal vulnerability in stash.py pop() that allows attackers to write arbitrary files outside the worktree through intermediate directory symlinks. Attackers can craft a malicious repository whose popped stash writes a payload into .git/hooks/post-checkout, achieving code execution on the next checkout.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:37:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:37:01", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jelmer/dulwich/security/advisories/GHSA-cm62-gvxx-vmxx", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dulwich-0.22.5-before-1.2.8-path-traversal-via-stash-pop-symlinks"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114098", "GHSA-mw9m-763w-f8m9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a3ba12cc-5170-3785-882c-8dbbfd251401", "product": {"name": "dulwich", "vendor": {"name": "jelmer"}}, "product_version": "0.22.5 <1.2.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "61e70841-ae21-3a5d-8974-c30f1bc1f64c", "vendor": {"name": "jelmer"}}], "isExploited": false}